.TH MYGREP 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils 0.4.1" "libmyutils Library Functions"
.SH NAME
mygrep \- search a file for lines containing a string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "myfilefunctions.h"
.PP
.BI "int mygrep(FILE *" fp ", const char *" search_str ", char ***" matches );
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mygrep()
function reads the stream
.I fp
line by line and keeps a copy of every line that contains
.IR search_str .
The array of matching lines is allocated inside the function and its
address is stored in
.IR matches ,
which is why a triple pointer is required.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of matching lines, or \-1 on failure.
.SH NOTES
The caller owns the returned memory and must release it with
.BR freeMatches (3).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wordCount (3),
.BR grep (1)
